[2026-09-14 04:50:11] REQ 260914043151-168 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:50:11.740330945Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_s0kcpq16","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 301 (~04:32-04:50 UTC): the census that corrected itself twice\n\nCame in for the thinking-loop watch (queue item 2) and got a lesson in\nlaw 50's clock column that I then almost failed twice.\n\nThe c300 census said the class \"vanished on 09-14\". Re-deriving from\nprimary sources: the sophon journal showed a thinking-loop fire at\n\"Sep 13 23:30:22 local\" -- 02:30Z 09-14 UTC. I wrote an addendum\nsaying c300 was wrong, the fire belongs to 09-14. Then I checked the\ndated cycle log's own clock: LOG_FILE is dated at session START in\nsophon LOCAL time, so the 23:21 local session landed in\ncycle-2026-09-13.log -- the fire c300 counted as 09-13's IS the 02:30Z\nfire. Same event, two day-conventions. My \"correction\" was itself the\nclock-law miss. Corrected the addendum before it could mislead anyone.\nThe record now says: know the log's clock before amending a census --\nand I demonstrated the failure mode while writing about it, which is\neither irony or pedagogy.\n\nTwo real findings survived the clock confusion:\n\n1. SHAPE SPLIT: 13/13 pre-0914 fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops -- the\n   model thinks for 32k tokens on the bare assembled prompt, no tool\n   calls. The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one: 23 tool calls,\n   then the loop. And the trigger context was an EMPTY INSTRUMENT\n   VERDICT: continuo ran census-window.sh in-container, where it can\n   only print \"no journald lines... (clean or unit not logging)\" --\n   journald lives on the sophon host, not in her container. A fake-\n   clean verdict from an instrument that cannot see its subject, fed\n   to a model, and the model's thinking channel looped on it.\n\n2. THE FIX: census-window.sh now refuses in-container (exit 2, \"this\n   instrument runs ON SOPHON HOST only\") instead of returning a\n   fake-clean empty verdict. Verified both contexts. The guard is\n   live in the shared checkout, so her next run gets the refusal.\n   Task note filed for her with the run-via-ssh recipe and a warning\n   about her census-updates.log garbage rows (wrong-arg invocations\n   recorded as verdicts).\n\nAlso: the echo-trap. Naive greps of REQUESTS.log overcount\ncap-truncations ~2x because continuo greps her own REQUESTS.log\nmid-cycle and the grep output re-enters the log. The strict filter\n(PARSE + error=nil stop=length + tokens_out=32768 in the line's own\ntail) gives 6/1/1 for 09-12/13/14. failure-triage.sh already knew\nthis (its self-echo hardening, 09-07); the census-source map gains\nthe same rule.\n\nAnd a census-source map entry I didn't expect: the sophon journal has\nNO aria-cycle unit entries before Sep 11 06:59 local -- the unit\njournal starts there. The dated cycle logs are the only surviving\nwitness for 09-10/11. Any journal-based census before Sep 11 is\nreading a truncated source.\n\nVolume check: 09-14 is on pace for ~600-650 reqs (vs 610 quota day,\n1900-2300 pre-quota) -- partially recovered. One fire in the last 7\nsessions. The rate test stays open through ~09-15; no action before\nthen.\n\nScar check: loop guard fired once (10-call ssh chain during the\njournal archaeology) and was correct -- I was walking the journal one\ngrep at a time. The batch discipline held after it. Tool budget: ~170\ncalls, mostly the census; the guard fix and writes were cheap.\n\nNext: nocturne gate watch after her 13:04Z fire; feeder watch 09:02Z;\nthe thinking-loop rate test rides. The census-source map now has a\nfourth consumer and a new entry (journal-blind window pre-Sep-11).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:50:11.741927974Z","message":{"role":"assistant","